PagerSMPTd is installed.

Configure it:

  1) cp /usr/local/etc/pagersmtpd.env.sample /usr/local/etc/pagersmtpd.env
     edit PAGER_DOMAIN (required), PAGER_URL, SHARE_URL, limits

  2) sysrc pagersmtpd_enable=YES
     service pagersmtpd start

  3) For an MX on a real interface, point the domain's MX at this host and
     forward port 25 to the service (SMTP_PORT defaults to 8025 so the daemon
     runs unprivileged). Example pf rule for a jail / port redirect:

       rdr on $ext_if inet proto tcp from any to ($ext_if) port 25 \
           -> 127.0.0.1 port 8025

The service runs as the unprivileged user "pager" (uid/gid 10000). Override
with: sysrc pagersmtpd_uid=... pagersmtpd_gid=... pagersmtpd_user=...
